diepxuan (5.8.7+ppa~1) noble; urgency=medium

  * chore(cleanup): delete all 17 remaining bash files in src/var/lib
    (1,591 lines). None was ever packaged: src/debian/ductn.install only
    copies src/ductn/var/lib/lxc/hooks/default-hook.sh, so the whole tree
    was dead code carried in the repo. Every file was audited first, and
    any behaviour missing from Python was ported before deletion. Details
    in docs/SALVAGE-5.8.7.md.
  * fix(git): `git:detrack` ran `git rm --cached`, which removes the file
    from the index; the bash original ran
    `git update-index --no-assume-unchanged`. Users of the Python version
    may have dropped files from their repos. `git:untrack` was an alias to
    detrack and now issues `--assume-unchanged` itself.
  * fix(git): `git:viewuntrack` read `git status --short` and filtered
    untracked `??` entries, i.e. a different set of files. It now parses
    `git ls-files -v` and keeps the lines tagged with a lowercase letter,
    matching `grep "^[[:lower:]]"` in bash.
  * fix(git): `git:tag:cleanup` only printed the tag list. It now keeps the
    newest N tags (default 5), deletes the rest on origin and prunes.
  * fix(git): `git:configure --global` was missing half of the bash setup.
    Added core.fileMode=false, core.autocrlf=false, core.eol=lf, gc.auto=0,
    receive.denyCurrentBranch=updateInstead, and generation of ~/.gitignore
    with core.excludesfile pointing at it.
  * fix(disk): `disk:check` ran `smartctl -a /dev/sda` for all three
    "sector size" modes. The bash original measures sequential write
    throughput with dd (8k x 10k = 80 MB, 512k x 1k = 512 MB). Ported the
    dd profiles and parse MB/s from stderr; SMART moved to `disk:health`.
  * fix(php): `php:composer:install` executed the installer without
    verifying it. Bash downloads the SHA384 from
    composer.github.io/installer.sig and compares; Python carried a
    "# Verify signature (skip for now)" comment. Now verified, and the
    installer is fetched into a tmpdir instead of $HOME.
  * fix(os): `os:codename`, `os:release` and `os:distro` returned empty on
    macOS because the distro module reads /etc/os-release, which does not
    exist there. Added a darwin branch using `sw_vers`, as the deleted
    macos/os.sh did.
  * fix(zfs): the old `zfs:disk:replace_boot_disk` called
    `zpool replace <pool> <new_disk>`, missing the `-part3` suffix and the
    sgdisk steps, so it could not work on a real boot disk. It now
    delegates to `zfs:disk:replace:boot` and warns that it is deprecated.
  * test: repair two permanently failing tests. test_modules.py still
    expected utils.user (removed in 5.6.4) and test_cli_output.py still
    expected a `cli:tmux:install` line (removed in 5.6.6). The suite goes
    from 182 tests / 2 failures to 303 tests / 0 failures.
  * feat(style): new src/utils/style.py with the ANSI palette and status
    glyphs salvaged from environment.color.sh and environment.text.sh,
    exposing ok()/fail()/info() and disabling colour when stdout is not a
    tty or NO_COLOR is set.
  * feat(mssql): migrate mssql.sh (230 lines) to src/utils/mssql.py. The
    repository setup is rewritten with a keyring under /etc/apt/keyrings
    and signed-by, because apt-key was removed in Debian 12 / Ubuntu 24.04
    (the package targets noble). Adds sqlsrv:apt, sqlsrv:install,
    sqlsrv:php:install|enable|disable and the legacy mssql:* aliases.
    `sqlsrv:ad:spn` is not ported: it mixed PowerShell and ktpass and
    embedded a domain password in argv. Kept as docs/MSSQL-AD-SPN.md.
  * feat(fleet): new `fleet:status` reads the FQDN and ductn version of
    each host over SSH and reports version drift, salvaged from the
    inventory half of main.sh. The WireGuard provisioning half is dropped:
    it hardcoded 10.8.x.x, derived addresses from the Proxmox VMID, and
    depended on the removed host.sh helpers.
  * feat(completion): new `completion:path <tool>` and
    `completion:exists <tool>`, collapsing six near-duplicate bash
    functions into one command with an argument. The angular -> angular2
    quirk is preserved.
  * feat(macos): port wireguard and sshfs management from macos/wg.sh and
    macos/sshfs.sh (`wg:*`, 10 commands; `sshfs:*`, 5 commands). The
    sshfs plist no longer hardcodes one machine's remote path and key;
    both come from arguments and $DUCTN_SSHFS_IDENTITY. `wg:hotfix`
    (an unconditional `while true; sleep 5` DNS loop) and `wg:fix` are
    intentionally not ported; WG_QUICK_DNS_SKIP=1 covers the same problem.
  * feat(zfs): add `zfs:disk:replace:disk <pool> <old> <new>` for a failed
    disk in a RAIDZ or mirror pool, `zfs:disk:replace:boot <old> <new>`
    (sgdisk -R, sgdisk -G, then zpool replace on -part3), and
    `zfs:disk:format:boot:disk <partition>` running proxmox-boot-tool
    format/init behind a confirmation prompt.
  * feat: add `vm:agent:install` (alias pve:vm), `vm:command <json>`,
    `file:chmod`, `file:chmod:files`, `file:chmod:dirs`, `hash:md5`,
    `ssh <host> <command>`, `dns:set`, `dns:status`, `log:config:store`
    and `log:config:mssql`, all salvaged from the files being deleted.
  * feat(docs): add docs/MSSQL-AD-SPN.md and docs/SALVAGE-5.8.7.md, and
    rewrite TASKS.md, which still listed eleven completed tasks as pending
    and two deliberately dropped ones as outstanding.
  * test: add 121 tests covering the salvaged code (test_style.py,
    test_helpers.py, test_git_utils.py, test_mssql.py, test_salvage.py)
    and rewrite test_disk.py for the dd-based disk:check.

